# P084 gate working notes (US customs-duty / duty-mitigation services) - started 2026-10-18
Status: init. Ideas: 1 Intercompany Reconciler, 2 Rights Ledger, 3 Origin Rail, 4 Licence Bank, 5 Second Filer, 6 Peer Ledger, 7 Weight Line, 8 Pass-Through
(Notes appended per idea; backup made after each. Backups: gate/backups/P084/)
Usage cap note: user capped weekly usage at 92%; notes are written incrementally so nothing is lost if the run stops.


## Cross-cutting
- Pool: $214B TTM US customs duties (drorpoleg tracker, secondary). Census related-party 2025: 49.0% ($1,663.1B of $3,391.2B) imports, report 7 Jul 2026. https://www.census.gov/foreign-trade/Press-Release/related_party/rp25.pdf (via search summary). Importers identified 2023: 242,515, falling to 239,231 in 2024 (Census profile).

## Idea 1 Intercompany Reconciler (searches done: 5)
- Premise real: CBP HQ W548314 (2012) lets post-importation TP adjustments count if written policy predates imports; reconciliation (21 months) is "strongly encouraged" vehicle. Sources: PwC https://www.pwc.com/us/en/tax-services/publications/insights/assets/pwc-how-post-importation-tp-adj-could-impact-us-customs-value-rept.pdf ; STR Trade https://www.strtrade.com/trade-news-resources/str-trade-report/trade-report/march/savings-strategies-reconciliation-and-transfer-pricing ; FTI https://www.fticonsulting.com/insights/service-sheets/customs-valuation-related-party-pricing
- Gap evidence: KPMG 2020 TP/trade survey (100+ cos): only 54.5% made customs valuation adjustments after TP adjustment. https://kpmg.com/kpmg-us/content/dam/kpmg/pdf/2020/2020-transfer-pricing-trade-compliance-survey.pdf
- COMPETITOR (software): Optravis (msg group, founded 2014, acquired 2021), operational-TP SaaS with customs + anti-dumping rules in the engine, SAP R3/S4 ERP connectors, Henkel customer. https://www.msg.group/en/surplus/henkel-scaling-transfer-pricing/ ; https://intuitionlabs.ai/software/finance-accounting/transfer-pricing-for-pharma/optravis . Pitch said "found none": WRONG, partial overlap (no ACE filing arm).
- GingerControl blog on TP+customs; sells PO-to-entry reconciliation service per entity (not TP pricing). https://gingercontrol.com/blog/transfer-pricing-customs-valuation
- Big Four / Forvis Mazars publish "aligning customs valuations and transfer prices" playbooks (Mar 2025): https://www.forvismazars.us/forsights/2025/03/tariffs-got-you-down-aligning-customs-valuations-transfer-prices ; Alston Mar 2026 on 482/1059A: https://www.alston.com/en/insights/publications/2026/03/irs-interaction-sections-482-1059a ; PLR 202552012 is taxpayer-specific (deductive-value; basis not capped) https://ezel.ai/irs-rulings/202552012
- Premise caution: a lower import price shifts profit to US = US tax up, parent-country authority fights (Japan NTA/Korea NTS/Germany). Downward adjustment invented after the fact fails W548314. So "2% defensible reduction" is optimistic; already the standard LRD tariff-sharing play since 2018.
- Fee-bar premise: 17 CFR 210.2-01(c)(5) (SEC contingent-fee ban for audit clients) is real but narrow: only SEC-audit-client groups; non-Big-Four firms (Sandler Travis, Livingston, BDO/Crowe/RSM) can take contingency.
- Pool sizing: Census gives no group-concentration; Census LFTTD needed. Top-importer concentration: large importers 2/3 of known import value.
- Prelim verdict: WEAK. median ~$12M, upside ~$60M.
